{
 "title": "A town's greenhouse gas inventory and its measures (invented)",
 "about": "An invented town of 320,000 residents (Ardel, as in the programmes cohort) with an inventory for 2024 in the structure of the Global Protocol for Community-Scale Greenhouse Gas Emission Inventories: homes, commerce and industry burning gas and using grid power with its losses, a plant within the town supplying the grid, cars, electric railways, flights, landfill elsewhere, incineration (some of it a neighbour's waste), wastewater, refrigerants, soils, and livestock not estimated; and seven measures with yearly costs. Every activity, factor, uncertainty, measure, cost and target is invented to show the tools and says so; the potentials are the IPCC's AR6.",
